CC   IMGT/LIGM-DB annotation level: by annotators
CC   
CC   This sequence spans the recombination junction of the translocation
CC   product of chromosomes 15 and 12. [1] calls this 12;15 product M
CC   and the 15;12 reciprocal product R. This sequence contains a 106 bp
CC   repeat (bases 19-124) from the c-myc oncogene, which occurred in
CC   translocation. Thus, the same sequence occurs in the 15;12
CC   translocation. There is also a 1.6 kb deletion in the C-alpha
CC   sequence.
CC   The two genes are situated in opposite transcriptional orientation.
CC   [1] also reports reciprocal translocation sequences from three
CC   other plasmacytomas. [1] suggests that viable switch sequences play
CC   a role in the trantlocation mechanism.
